      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Vascular inflammation, particularly aortitis, is a known rare manifestation of ankylosing spondylitis. This condition has not been reported to date in the coronary circulation. We present the first documented case of a coronary aneurysm in a patient with ankylosing spondylitis. This association may limit treatment options in such patients, as newer drug-eluting stents may potentiate degeneration in established aneurysmal coronary arteries."},
